<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<rdf:RDF
         xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
         xmlns:foaf="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/"
         xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
         xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
         xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"
         xmlns:games="https://example.org/schema/games">

         <games:simulation-strategy rdf:about="https://dbpedia.org/page/Cities:_Skylines">
         <games:number>2</games:number>
         <games:abstract>	
            Cities: Skylines is a city-building simulation game developed by Colossal Order and published by Paradox Interactive. The game was released in 2015 and offers players the opportunity to design and manage their own cities.
            It is known for its extensive modding community and support for user-generated content.
         </games:abstract>        
         <games:developer>Colossal_Order</games:developer>
         <games:releaseDate>2015-03-10</games:releaseDate>
         <games:platforms>Microsoft Windows, MacOS, Xbox One, PlayStation 4</games:platforms>
         <foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf rdf:resource="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cities:_Skylines"/>
         </games:simulation-strategy>

         <games:simulation-strategy rdf:about="https://dbpedia.org/page/Planet_Coaster">
         <games:number>3</games:number>
         <games:abstract>	
            Planet Coaster is a construction and management simulation video game developed and published by Frontier Developments. The game was released in 2016 and allows players to design and manage their own theme parks.
            It is known for its detailed customization options and creative possibilities.
         </games:abstract>        
         <games:developer>Frontier_Developments</games:developer>
         <games:releaseDate>2016-11-17</games:releaseDate>
         <games:platforms>Microsoft Windows, MacOS, Xbox One, PlayStation 4</games:platforms>
         <foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf rdf:resource="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Planet_Coaster"/>
         </games:simulation-strategy>

         <games:simulation-strategy rdf:about="https://dbpedia.org/page/Flight_Simulator_X">
         <games:number>4</games:number>
         <games:abstract>	
            Microsoft Flight Simulator X is a flight simulation video game developed by Microsoft Game Studios and ACES Studio. The game was originally released in 2006 and offers players the chance to pilot a wide variety of aircraft in realistic environments.
         </games:abstract>        
         <games:developer>Microsoft_Game_Studios</games:developer>
         <games:releaseDate>2006-10-17</games:releaseDate>
         <games:platforms>Microsoft Windows</games:platforms>
         <foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf rdf:resource="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Flight_Simulator_X"/>
         </games:simulation-strategy>  

         <games:simulation-strategy rdf:about="https://dbpedia.org/page/Two_Point_Hospital">
         <games:number>5</games:number>
         <games:abstract>	
            Two Point Hospital is a business simulation video game developed by Two Point Studios and published by Sega. The game was released in 2018 and allows players to manage and operate their own healthcare facilities.
            It combines humor with strategic management gameplay.
         </games:abstract>        
         <games:developer>Two_Point_Studios</games:developer>
         <games:releaseDate>2018-08-30</games:releaseDate>
         <games:platforms>Microsoft Windows, MacOS, Xbox One, PlayStation 4</games:platforms>
         <foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf rdf:resource="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Two_Point_Hospital"/>
         </games:simulation-strategy>           
         
         <games:simulation-strategy rdf:about="https://dbpedia.org/page/The_Escapists_2">
         <games:number>6</games:number>
         <games:abstract>	
            The Escapists 2 is a strategy role-playing video game developed by Mouldy Toof Studios and published by Team17. The game was released in 2017 and is set in a prison environment.
            Players must plan and execute prison escapes while dealing with daily routines.
         </games:abstract>        
         <games:developer>Mouldy_Toof_Studios</games:developer>
         <games:releaseDate>2017-08-22</games:releaseDate>
         <games:platforms>Microsoft Windows, MacOS, Xbox One, PlayStation 4</games:platforms>
         <foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf rdf:resource="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Escapists_2"/>
         </games:simulation-strategy>           
         
         <games:simulation-strategy rdf:about="https://dbpedia.org/page/RollerCoaster_Tycoon">
         <games:number>7</games:number>
         <games:abstract>	
            RollerCoaster Tycoon is a construction and management simulation video game developed by Chris Sawyer Productions and published by Hasbro Interactive. The game was originally released in 1999.
            Players can design and operate their own amusement parks, including creating custom roller coasters.
         </games:abstract>        
         <games:developer>Chris_Sawyer_Productions</games:developer>
         <games:releaseDate>1999-03-31</games:releaseDate>
         <games:platforms>Microsoft Windows</games:platforms>
         <foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf rdf:resource="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RollerCoaster_Tycoon"/>
         </games:simulation-strategy>           
         
         <games:simulation-strategy rdf:about="https://dbpedia.org/page/SimCity_4">
         <games:number>8</games:number>
         <games:abstract>	
            SimCity 4 is a city-building simulation video game developed by Maxis and published by Electronic Arts. The game was released in 2003 and offers players the opportunity to create and manage their own cities.
         </games:abstract>        
         <games:developer>Maxis</games:developer>
         <games:releaseDate>2003-01-14</games:releaseDate>
         <games:platforms>Microsoft Windows, MacOS</games:platforms>
         <foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf rdf:resource="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SimCity_4"/>
         </games:simulation-strategy>           

         <games:simulation-strategy rdf:about="https://dbpedia.org/page/Anno_1800">
         <games:number>9</games:number>
         <games:abstract>	
            Anno 1800 is a city-building real-time strategy video game developed by Blue Byte and published by Ubisoft. The game was released in 2019 and is set during the Industrial Revolution.
            Players must build and manage cities, trade, and explore new territories.
         </games:abstract>        
         <games:developer>Blue_Byte</games:developer>
         <games:releaseDate>2019-04-16</games:releaseDate>
         <games:platforms>Microsoft Windows</games:platforms>
         <foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf rdf:resource="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anno_1800"/>
         </games:simulation-strategy>           

         <games:simulation-strategy rdf:about="https://dbpedia.org/page/The_Settlers_IV">
         <games:number>10</games:number>
         <games:abstract>	
            The Settlers IV is a real-time strategy video game developed by Blue Byte and published by Ubisoft. The game was originally released in 2001 and focuses on city-building and resource management.
         </games:abstract>        
         <games:developer>Blue_Byte</games:developer>
         <games:releaseDate>2001-02-15</games:releaseDate>
         <games:platforms>Microsoft Windows</games:platforms>
         <foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf rdf:resource="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Settlers_IV"/>
         </games:simulation-strategy>
</rdf:RDF>
